From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:38:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] feat: download the whole mailbox in the background

Upstream keeps only the newest 50 messages of each folder, so search and the
list never see older mail. A worker (backfill.py) now fetches every header of
every real folder, then every body, newest first, on its own IMAP and SQLite
connections, and never notifies. Bodies move to their own table (a mid-row
BLOB made every list walk gigabytes of overflow pages), the list reads the
database a page at a time and grows on scroll, and regrouping threads is
skipped while grouping is off.
